⍝ doc 2   [hum sbl] := [spec sbl] or [bin sbl]
⍝ line:   <hum> := <rhs> | <rhs> | …  ; <role>        role: class | value | literal | infixl P | infixr P | infix P | prefix P
⍝ several right-hand sides form an overload set: the class checker picks the one that fits the arguments.
⍝ a right-hand side made only of 1 0 . is a bin symbol (a numeral); everything else is a spec symbol.
⍝ ---- syntax words of the human reader (built into its grammar; listed here because they are notation too)
:= := ≔ ; syntax
in := ∶ ; syntax
subseteq := ⊆ ; syntax
|-> := ↦ ; syntax
-> := → ; syntax
